{"id": "EUVD-2026-81749", "enisaUuid": "a56e7e90-1e6e-36d8-a447-8bb245220829", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: safely discard unregistered deferred locks\n\nWhen vfs_lock_file() defers a lock, smb2_lock() puts its ksmbd_lock on\nrollback_list before allocating and registering the asynchronous work.\nIf either operation fails, rollback assumes that smb_lock->conn is\ninitialized and dereferences NULL. The deferred file_lock also remains\nlinked into the VFS blocked-lock state while it is freed.\n\nKeep the lock off rollback_list until async setup succeeds. On setup\nfailures, explicitly unblock and wake the deferred lock before freeing it\nand its ksmbd wrapper.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:06:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:50:12", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ecdcfa15b3d799476c685cecd433ebefc93015c8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/77413400f083a959724de6f36348c9677ef9873a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/52b91bc5253bb83665f3ea70565d0b2487dae643", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d09af9a35ff7b77a950b507133d9092aadbfeff4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/054bcca4cd9f00719b01f7108b51a2168fb94f15"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7qq9-mrjw-5hqq", "CVE-2026-90156"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "091c8529-e443-3a93-aa77-6f4b6d9fb8cb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "0bed8c21-ea6a-3e2d-9ac7-71719c44c035", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e2f34481b24db2fd634b5edb0a5bd0e4d38cc6e9 <77413400f083a959724de6f36348c9677ef9873a"}, {"id": "332f59cf-dd2a-397d-9dc8-9cbd5326a78a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e2f34481b24db2fd634b5edb0a5bd0e4d38cc6e9 <d09af9a35ff7b77a950b507133d9092aadbfeff4"}, {"id": "5001fceb-0663-37d7-98ba-ab674bf4b4d4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e2f34481b24db2fd634b5edb0a5bd0e4d38cc6e9 <52b91bc5253bb83665f3ea70565d0b2487dae643"}, {"id": "553a52c6-d178-3230-a2e6-275837cf98ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "74e85221-c9e2-3148-a1d2-376f9f39b18d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "9528ebeb-32b9-3595-bd6d-07c2ab962996", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "aa5297a2-7d54-3f7a-9ad9-ebd7ddfcdb17", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e2f34481b24db2fd634b5edb0a5bd0e4d38cc6e9 <ecdcfa15b3d799476c685cecd433ebefc93015c8"}, {"id": "c4409bd0-8e48-3edb-ab38-1ff46ea82f55", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "d0a6af4f-b0b0-3084-9e38-c748435a2253", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "de1e5938-b4fa-3a2f-a194-40a45239265c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15"}, {"id": "f59ec8c8-8666-35ef-8e73-f1c080365b0e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e2f34481b24db2fd634b5edb0a5bd0e4d38cc6e9 <054bcca4cd9f00719b01f7108b51a2168fb94f15"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "37319502-4e7a-3657-9446-858067661f79", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}